@startuml
title MARS-OPS Mission Lifecycle (class Mission, enum MissionStatus)
skinparam shadowing false

[*] --> PENDING : new Mission(...)

PENDING --> ASSIGNED : submitMission() accepted\n[no other active mission\nand environment allows start\nand every agent isReady() and canPerform()\nand colony resources sufficient]\n/ agents.setAvailability(false), resources consumed

PENDING --> FAILED : submitMission() rejected\n/ failMission(reason)\n(another mission active, environment blocks start,\nagent missing or not registered, agent cannot operate,\nresources insufficient, agent not ready,\nagent lacks capability)\nnever becomes active

ASSIGNED --> IN_PROGRESS : first time unit\nColony.advanceTime()\n/ startMission(), onMissionStart() on every agent

ASSIGNED --> FAILED : failMission(reason)

IN_PROGRESS --> IN_PROGRESS : advanceTime()\n[progress + 1 < duration]\n/ progress++

IN_PROGRESS --> COMPLETED : advanceTime()\n[progress >= duration]\n/ complete(), releaseAgents()

IN_PROGRESS --> FAILED : failMission(reason)\n[agent cannot operate in environment\n(dust storm, communication disruption)\nor agent not usable (battery 0, damage)]\n/ releaseAgents()

COMPLETED --> [*]
FAILED --> [*]

note right of FAILED
  Failed missions are never retried.
  A new Mission object must be created.
end note

note left of PENDING
  PENDING is the extra initial state.
  It guarantees a rejected mission
  never passes through ASSIGNED.
end note
@enduml
